WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.860
Ten boats share one fishing ground.

2
00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:06.730
Nobody owns the fish, and
nobody can keep a boat out.

3
00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:11.080
Every captain knows that a fish
caught today can't breed tomorrow.

4
00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:14.290
Every captain wants
plenty of fish next year.

5
00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:16.460
Yet the stock keeps shrinking.

6
00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:19.430
Off New England, all four
Atlantic cod stocks were

7
00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:22.230
rated overfished in 2024.

8
00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:24.790
So why do fishers who all want fish next

9
00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:27.630
year still empty the sea this year?

10
00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:30.840
In this mission, you'll
follow one extra catch and see

11
00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.110
who gains and who pays.

12
00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:35.300
Then you'll use a graph lab to find how

13
00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.740
much the whole fleet should catch.

14
00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:42.920
Your mission: explain how an open-access
resource ends up overconsumed.
